We've worked on two reports related to the Medford Historic District.

421
00:29:13,350 --> 00:29:19,875
One was on establishing local historic districts, basically a strategies report for creating new local historic districts.

422
00:29:21,456 --> 00:29:25,239
And then we worked upon a administrative staff assistance report.

423
00:29:25,259 --> 00:29:33,224
We talked about the options related to staff assistance for Medford and preparing to other

424
00:29:35,297 --> 00:29:36,738
cities and towns in the area as well.

425
00:29:36,758 --> 00:29:46,164
So I'm going to start off just a few slides on establishing local historic district strategies report.

426
00:29:46,264 --> 00:29:53,769
Basics of local historic districts statewide level, we've got about 120 or so cities and towns of the local historic district.

427
00:29:57,331 --> 00:30:03,835
They've been around since the 1950s, but most of the local historic districts follow state law like we do.

428
00:30:04,315 --> 00:30:05,855
And that law was passed in 1960.

429
00:30:07,876 --> 00:30:13,797
And so that law, Mass General Law Chapter 3C, requires a two-thirds majority vote of city council.

430
00:30:14,617 --> 00:30:19,598
So the bar is pretty high to establish a local park, just like dumping.

431
00:30:20,278 --> 00:30:28,939
It would be a two-thirds majority vote of city council.

432
00:30:28,959 --> 00:30:31,460
I'm trying to think about some ways to make it a little bit easier.

433
00:30:34,870 --> 00:30:56,181
to pursue local historic districts, think about some strategies for how you as a historic district commission, when you recognize that a local historic district is needed, try to think about some strategies to go about primarily how to make your job a little easier.

434
00:30:56,241 --> 00:31:02,745
How do you make it a little less challenging for you as members of the commission?

435
00:31:03,913 --> 00:31:16,483
So one thing is just to think about addressing the misinformation and the myths that are out there, and to really focus on the benefits of local expansion.

436
00:31:16,563 --> 00:31:25,831
I mean, the real benefit is the idea that where you live, you will protect the place that you invest in.

437
00:31:26,391 --> 00:31:30,594
That neighborhood is not going to be destroyed next year or the year after that.

438
00:31:31,435 --> 00:31:32,456
So one of the big myths that

439
00:31:33,506 --> 00:31:35,147
than any other is the one on the bottom.

440
00:31:35,767 --> 00:31:40,689
I want to be able to paint my house any color I want.

441
00:31:41,809 --> 00:31:59,956
So that myth directly just in a public space or fly or something like that, explaining what the role of the commission is, how paint is going to be handled and how the other kinds of things that are exempt from review and things like that.

442
00:32:03,888 --> 00:32:13,951
So a good little brochure that really puts it right out there, proactively puts it out there in terms of what local historic districts are and what local historic districts are not.

443
00:32:14,191 --> 00:32:25,915
Next thing is really thinking about how you connect the top corners of a proposed local historic district.

444
00:32:26,715 --> 00:32:30,656
It's really good to try to think about neighborhood meetings, just sort of

445
00:32:32,079 --> 00:32:37,520
informal ways that you meet with property owners and talk about local history.

446
00:32:38,901 --> 00:32:53,904
Just sort of really preliminary discussions with neighborhoods so that they can get a sense of, again, the myths that are out there, the misinformation, and understanding what a local historic is, how it would benefit them.

447
00:33:01,103 --> 00:33:02,765
And this is a really big one.

448
00:33:03,345 --> 00:33:05,567
