564
00:45:52,515 --> 00:45:59,981
There's more local historic districts that get established every year or local historic districts that get expanded.

565
00:46:00,061 --> 00:46:06,125
So you might have a local historic district, but every few years, sometimes it gets expanded.

566
00:46:07,186 --> 00:46:18,655
So yeah, there's new ones coming up every year, but you're not unlike other commissions that I work with that,

567
00:46:22,008 --> 00:46:29,471
that definitely have, are dealing with some tension, conflicts related to creating new local historic districts.

568
00:46:30,131 --> 00:46:35,013
So that's a normal aspect of local historic districts as well.

569
00:46:35,673 --> 00:46:46,177
And then regarding single house historic districts, I mean, we were told way back when that that was maybe a less than effective method at the,

570
00:46:46,913 --> 00:46:50,234
mass historical, you know, didn't like that or whatever.

571
00:46:50,334 --> 00:47:01,917
Is that still the case or, I mean, I love the idea and we seem to have much better luck with single house districts with people supporting them from ownership on down.

572
00:47:01,977 --> 00:47:07,799
So, I mean, is that a realistic method to approach it in a smaller scale?

573
00:47:10,600 --> 00:47:11,560
Yeah, so a couple of things.

574
00:47:12,680 --> 00:47:14,421
I mean, I think if you can,

575
00:47:15,553 --> 00:47:18,314
try to think about protecting neighborhoods, I think that's ideal.

576
00:47:19,814 --> 00:47:24,435
But I think there's a lot of reason to do single building local historic districts as well.

577
00:47:25,516 --> 00:47:29,537
Right next door Somerville, Somerville has 200 single building local historic districts.

578
00:47:29,557 --> 00:47:34,118
So they've been doing this technique since the 1980s.

579
00:47:35,938 --> 00:47:38,279
So they're definitely around.

580
00:47:38,799 --> 00:47:41,760
And then the other important thing with single building local historic districts is,

581
00:47:42,676 --> 00:47:46,358
Uh, it's actually very common to do this around the country.

582
00:47:46,718 --> 00:47:47,338
Very common.

583
00:47:47,818 --> 00:47:49,639
You're probably going to, I'm going to use a different term though.

584
00:47:49,659 --> 00:47:51,360
And you'd be like, oh, that's the same thing.

585
00:47:51,840 --> 00:47:52,841
Local landmark.

586
00:47:53,981 --> 00:47:54,261
Yeah.

587
00:47:54,722 --> 00:47:58,343
Local landmark is basically the same thing as a single building, local historic district.

588
00:47:58,764 --> 00:48:03,065
If you go pretty much anywhere around the country, they're going to use the term local landmark.

589
00:48:03,546 --> 00:48:08,368
And it just happens that maybe we, because we were one of the early adopters of a state law.

590
00:48:08,967 --> 00:48:12,708
for local historic districts, it did not include the word local landmark.

